{"chunk_id": "f454e69c9002", "text": "Bharata, tormented by grief and loyalty, presses deeper into the forest to find his exiled brother Rama. Declaring he will know no peace until Rama is restored to the throne, he advances on foot with companions and eventually spots smoke from Rama\u2019s hermitage on Chitrakuta. Leaving the army behind, he hastens forward. Following signs left by Rama and Lakshmana, Bharata reaches the Mandakini and finally beholds the austere hermitage filled with weapons, ritual items, and forest implements. Inside he sees Rama seated like a radiant ascetic, with matted locks, bark garments, Sita and Lakshmana beside him. The sight overwhelms Bharata: he laments that the rightful king lives like a hermit because of him. Choked with grief and devotion, he rushes forward but collapses unconscious before reaching Rama, while Shatrughna weeps at their brother\u2019s feet.\nBharata reaches Rama\u2019s forest hermitage at Chitrakuta and, overwhelmed with grief and love, collapses while rushing to greet his exiled brother.\nThemes: brotherly devotion, exile and kingship, repentance and loyalty, ascetic life vs royalty, family reunion", "vector": [0.015413728542625904, -0.01838877983391285, -0.009315545670688152, -0.005428459029644728, -0.006889061536639929, 0.02840433642268181, -0.02765047736465931, -0.022508081048727036, -0.029642820358276367, -0.008615533821284771, 0.002370954491198063, 0.01735222339630127, 0.0009717716020531952, 0.01276175957173109, 0.013529079966247082, -0.006441457662731409, 0.05018548294901848, -0.013838700950145721, 0.03672371059656143, -0.01047325786203146, -0.010022289119660854, -0.010708838701248169, -0.004684696439653635, -0.0032055843621492386, -0.016638748347759247, -0.012176171876490116, 0.014875257387757301, -0.037154488265514374, 0.009248237125575542, -0.01200116891413927, -0.000994488364085555, -0.007027044426649809, -0.008077062666416168, -0.015373342670500278, -0.025563903152942657, 0.014188706874847412, -0.0042741